From: Gerard Torres <meganace07@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: uaccess: drop const from put_user register variable

With newer GCC a const-qualified local register variable can be
constant-propagated instead of being kept in r2, so the __asmeq()
checks in __put_user_x() fail with '.err encountered' (fork.c, futex.c,
sound/core, ...). Upstream dropped the qualifier as well.

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/uaccess.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/uaccess.h
index 7e1f7602..c38e7ce7 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/uaccess.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/uaccess.h
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ extern int __put_user_8(void *, unsigned long long);
 #define __put_user_check(x,p)							\
 	({								\
 		unsigned long __limit = current_thread_info()->addr_limit - 1; \
-		register const typeof(*(p)) __r2 asm("r2") = (x);	\
+		register typeof(*(p)) __r2 asm("r2") = (x);	\
 		register const typeof(*(p)) __user *__p asm("r0") = (p);\
 		register unsigned long __l asm("r1") = __limit;		\
 		register int __e asm("r0");				\
